config BR2_PACKAGE_SND_HDA_MACBOOKPRO
	bool "snd-hda-macbookpro"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	help
	  Sound output for Macs whose HD-audio codec is the Cirrus Logic
	  CS8409 with Apple's amplifiers: MacBookPro13,x and 14,x (2016
	  and 2017, no T2 chip) and the 2017-2019 iMacs. The kernel
	  binds its generic codec driver to that codec, which has no
	  volume or switch controls, so the speakers stay silent. This is
	  David Odin's snd_hda_macbookpro: the kernel's own patch_cs8409
	  with Apple's setup patched in, built out of tree as
	  snd-hda-codec-cs8409.ko and picked by the codec's vendor id.
	  Speaker and headphone output; the microphone does not work.
	  Selected by the IYAKKI "mac" variant only
	  (configs/iyakki_mac.fragment). GPL-2.0.

	  https://github.com/davidjo/snd_hda_macbookpro

comment "snd-hda-macbookpro needs a Linux kernel to be built (x86_64)"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
